1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:26,760
It's us!

2
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:27,620
Run!

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,700
It's fast!

4
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:37,720
Fun fact, red dragons can run up to 60 kilometers per hour!

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:38,700
That's fun!

6
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:41,000
It's fine, the terrain's slowing it down!

7
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,420
Up ahead, turn right!

8
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:52,640
Now we baited fire breath down this corridor!

9
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:57,680
Dragons store fuel in their bellies, and click their tongue to ignite it!

10
00:00:58,180 --> 00:00:59,600
For our own safety!

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,260
We have to make it exhaust all of its fuel!

12
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:06,140
It's tonguing!

13
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:07,820
Look out!

14
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:13,500
Such intense heat!

15
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,080
But...

16
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:23,420
We can handle it thanks to the pan and spells!

17
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:24,680
Yes!

18
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,680
We've got the...

19
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:29,360
Oh, no!

20
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,620
The heat from the pan...

21
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:33,620
It's spreading evenly...

22
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:35,880
Cut!

23
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:47,600
Oh, yeah, of course it's hot!

24
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:51,000
Since he was cooking with that pan every single day!

25
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,500
I assumed it would be able to repel dragon fire!

26
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:58,140
According to Namari, adamantine is supposed to block all attacks from a dragon!

27
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,140
I think she was making stuff up!

28
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:01,140
I think she was making stuff up!

29
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:02,140
Was not...

30
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:07,000
Here it comes!

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:07,520
Damn it!

32
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:09,060
I've got a change course!

33
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:09,920
Let's go back!

34
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,640
Hmm?

35
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:16,860
Huh?

36
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,400
What?

37
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
They're here?

38
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:21,460
Already?

39
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,700
But why?

40
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:27,040
I thought that we were supposed to stay split up!

41
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:29,340
Should I still do things according to plan?

42
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,800
Ah, fine then!

43
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:33,980
Here I go!

44
00:02:39,060 --> 00:03:09,040
Here I go!

45
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,360
Oh, my God!

46
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:26,220
Are you kidding me?

47
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:27,580
It didn't work!

48
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:29,860
Quiet!

49
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,860
Don't move!

50
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:43,620
The inverse scale's right there!

51
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:47,020
If I get a bit closer, it's mine!

52
00:03:47,020 --> 00:04:00,760
It made a run for it!

53
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:02,520
Damn it, Tensuke!

54
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:05,020
You're just a monster after...

55
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:05,700
Did you?

56
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:06,060
You two!

57
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:06,800
Get up!

58
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:07,360
Hurry!

59
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:08,980
Up up us!

60
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:11,620
Get under its belly!

61
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,200
Damn you, Elias!

62
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,540
Look, I'm sorry, okay?

63
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:15,940
Damn it!

64
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:18,540
The common language doesn't have enough curse words!

65
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:19,240
Punza!

66
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:19,920
Valo!

67
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:23,320
Please, don't cuss at me in a language I don't speak, Chilchak!

68
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,080
Any plans, genius?

69
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,600
Look really mad!

70
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:29,520
This way!

71
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:31,120
Let's run out the tail slide!

72
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,460
On second thought, nixed that.

73
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,560
This is where we live now, under the red dragon's crotch.

74
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:43,640
No good.

75
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,900
Simple spells aren't gonna work on it at all!

76
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:46,440
Focus!

77
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:58,220
What the hell was that?

78
00:04:58,220 --> 00:04:59,920
Did you just go and shatter our last weapon?

79
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,260
How do we fix this mess?

80
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:03,960
No choice.

81
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:05,520
Use this.

82
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:06,600
Huh?

83
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:09,860
Does this mean that knife is made from a special metal?

84
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:13,200
It cuts the bones and skin of any monster.

85
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:16,180
I've never gone a day without taking good care of it.

86
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:18,060
It's a mithril kitchen knife.

87
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,720
Maybe the only one of its kind in the world.

88
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,140
Mithril?

89
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,360
Seriously?

90
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:26,100
Wish we could have shown Namaari.

91
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:28,920
Pretty sure she would have killed Senshi if we had.

92
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:32,260
Yeah, I had a feeling that was the case, so I kept my mouth shut.

93
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:37,060
Take this!

94
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:38,580
Whoa!

95
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:40,760
It really pierced right through the scales!

96
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:49,440
But with the size of this blade, no matter where I stabbed, I doubt I'd be able to fatally wound it.

97
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:59,840
Oh, crap!

98
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:00,760
What now?

99
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,200
This means that the plan failed, doesn't it?

100
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:05,800
Or is this some sort of new one?

101
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:07,900
What the heck do I do?

102
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:12,380
There's no time to hesitate!

103
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:13,460
Stop!

104
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:14,360
Get back!

105
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:17,880
I'm getting farther from my sword.

106
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:21,680
We're gonna end up in the town square if we keep backing up.

107
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,920
And then we'll get burnt to a crisp!

108
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,720
I'll distract the dragon.

109
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:28,120
No, you can't!

110
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,160
Lyos, I know you know this.

111
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:34,320
Of all the monsters that we've eaten so far,

112
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:37,360
were there any that didn't fight until their last breath?

113
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:39,720
It's eat or be eaten here.

114
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:43,620
If we don't give it our all, then we're gonna be some monsters' dinner.

115
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:45,240
Here, prepare yourself!

116
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:47,620
Sensei!

117
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:00,620
No, stop!

118
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:03,100
There's no point in just running out there!

119
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:04,760
Go find Marcel!

120
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,300
You two think of a new plan!

121
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:09,060
Hey, are you alive?

122
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,140
I'll get this off!

123
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:10,640
Huh?

124
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:15,100
Can you move?

125
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:29,480
I did it!

126
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,360
Why is this thing stuck to the ground?

127
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:47,220
I'll be right back!

128
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,460
Come on!

129
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:50,760
Get up!

130
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,640
Sensei!

131
00:07:52,640 --> 00:08:04,980
Sorry, Marcel!

132
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,820
I didn't know you were here.

133
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:09,520
Uh, good to know that the spell is working.

134
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,320
What's going on?

135
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,200
Where are the others?

136
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:13,880
It's not looking too good.

137
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:16,040
All the plans we had set up failed.

138
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:19,120
The other two are still out there with the dragon.

139
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:19,620
Huh?

140
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,720
What should we do?

141
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,580
Does that mean we have to use my magic?

142
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,800
The dragon is wounded and violent.

143
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,300
It'll be too dangerous to get near it.

144
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,780
But we have to do something and fast.

145
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,220
Let's move upward.

146
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:33,840
Huh?

147
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:35,780
To do what?

148
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:38,060
We'll get level with the dragon's face.

149
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,300
And I'll get on the pan.

150
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,360
The pan?

151
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,860
And once I'm there, you'll blow it up.

152
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:44,220
What?

153
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:48,140
It's been blinded in its left eye.

154
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:52,840
So if we approach from that side, we should be able to jump on it without being noticed.

155
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,440
Are you sure?

156
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:58,660
Marcel, you did something similar before, didn't you?

157
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,320
Back when you fought the Undine.

158
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:04,260
Yeah, but at the time, I had water walking in water.

159
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:06,560
I have the pan and abjuration magic.

160
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:08,140
And then what?

161
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:11,260
How will you hit the inverse scale while clinging to its face?

162
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,060
Don't worry.

163
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,000
I've got an idea.

164
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:17,640
We can't make any more mistakes.

165
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,160
I've no intention to.

166
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:28,560
I'm a little hesitant that this is going to work, but...

167
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:31,140
I trust you.

168
00:09:31,140 --> 00:10:01,120
I'm a little hesitant.

169
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:02,660
You're going to get flung off.

170
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,500
Hurry and go through with the plan.

171
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,640
It'll be over fast.

172
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,220
It's not that big a deal.

173
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,060
Compared to what Valon went through.

174
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:13,700
This is nothing!

175
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,580
Lyos, no!

176
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:18,920
No!

177
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:18,980
No!

178
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:24,960
No!

179
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:34,240
No!

180
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:34,860
No!

181
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:35,120
No!

182
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:35,140
Okay.

183
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:35,340
No!

184
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:35,920
No!

185
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,980
No!

186
00:10:36,980 --> 00:11:06,960
I don't know.

187
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:36,960
I don't know.

188
00:11:36,980 --> 00:12:06,960
I don't know.

189
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,960
I don't know.

190
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,960
I don't know.

191
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,960
I don't know.

192
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,960
Help me.

193
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:17,260
So cold.

194
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:19,960
Can't breathe.

195
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:23,360
Rallin, run.

196
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:27,360
Bios!

197
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:35,360
Leave my brother...

198
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,360
alone!

199
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:53,360
The person in that grave there...

200
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:57,360
His ring is binding his soul here.

201
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,360
Please remove it.

202
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:01,360
The ghost will then be freed.

203
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,360
His ring?

204
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,360
Is this real?

205
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:09,360
This is the grave of Oldman who died recently.

206
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:13,360
When he was alive, he bragged about how he bought a golden ring from an elf.

207
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:17,360
But how would a child know about that?

208
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:21,360
Did I...

209
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:23,360
Do something bad?

210
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,360
No, you did great, Fallon.

211
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,360
Ghost magic is a cool talent to have.

212
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,360
Don't be sad.

213
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,360
Grownups are just scared of magic.

214
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:35,360
I think you should go and study it for real.

215
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:37,360
It'll help you get work, you know?

216
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:38,360
It will?

217
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,360
Probably.

218
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,360
You could try priest, grave keeper...

219
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:44,360
Ooh, traveling exorcist might be fun too.

220
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:50,360
You could wander across the lands and help people who need you.

221
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:52,360
Wow, I like that.

222
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:54,360
Would you be able to come with me too, brother?

223
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,360
Of course.

224
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:58,360
Where should we go first?

225
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,360
Hmm...

226
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:01,360
How about the ocean?

227
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:03,360
Ooh, or the desert!

228
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:04,360
I hear?

229
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,360
There's a country with talking dogs there.

230
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:08,360
Let's go, please!

231
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,360
But...

232
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:15,360
It might be best if we don't travel together anymore.

233
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,360
Fallon?

234
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,360
Why?

235
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:21,360
Don't worry about me.

236
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:25,360
Goodbye, big brother.

237
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,360
Lyos, you okay?

238
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:34,360
I stopped the bleeding for now, so hold on a bit longer.

239
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:37,360
I'll go find the other two, along with your leg!

240
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:42,360
Don't worry about me, huh?

241
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:46,360
You really shouldn't say such sad things.

242
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,360
I'm gonna bring you home.

243
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,360
I promise.

244
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,360
Hey!

245
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,360
Chill, Chuck!

246
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,360
Senshi!

247
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,360
Thank goodness!

248
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:02,360
You okay?

249
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,360
No, you're not.

250
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:08,360
I need more practice with my abjuration magic, huh?

251
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:11,360
We're still mostly in one piece, so it could be worse.

252
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:21,360
Motherfrog!

253
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:24,360
He's suffering more than before.

254
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:27,360
You get healing pains if you fix a big injury in a short time.

255
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,360
It's fine.

256
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,360
That just means it healed properly.

257
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,360
Now it's your turn, Senshi!

258
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,360
No, thanks.

259
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,360
I'll fix it myself.

260
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,360
But that'll take you months.

261
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:38,360
Fallon was always better at healing magic,

262
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:41,360
but I at least have the confidence of being able to heal quickly.

263
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,360
But...

264
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:45,360
Isn't that why it hurts so bad?

265
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,360
I found it!

266
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,360
Alright, let's begin.

267
00:15:54,360 --> 00:16:07,360
It's back on!

268
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:11,360
But now it itches.

269
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,360
Just those healing pains at work.

270
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:16,360
Lyos, you did well.

271
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:19,360
You really managed to slay the Red Dragon.

272
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:24,360
Thanks to all of you, it was possible cause we each did our part.

273
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,360
I felt like we weren't gonna make it at one point.

274
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:29,360
Even I was shaking in my boots.

275
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,360
Guess we underestimated it, didn't we?

276
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,360
Eh, doesn't matter since we won.

277
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,360
Although...

278
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:38,360
Here, Lyos.

279
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:40,360
Kensuke!

280
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,360
I still haven't forgiven you regarding that thing yet.

281
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:45,360
So we'll have a long talk later.

282
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,360
Hmm?

283
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,360
Alright.

284
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:49,360
Okay.

285
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,360
Let's go check inside of its stomach.

286
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,360
Such thick skin!

287
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:06,360
We wouldn't have even reached the fat underneath if we'd fought it with Senshi's knife.

288
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:10,360
Which means, getting to the stomach could take us a while.

289
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,360
Want me to blow it up?

290
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:13,360
Nah.

291
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:15,360
Dragon's organs should be similar to what other creatures have.

292
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:18,360
So let's try to carve our way through bit by bit.

293
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:28,360
I hit a rib bone.

294
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:30,360
We'll have to go around it and keep on digging.

295
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:35,360
It's dark.

296
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:36,360
Should we light a lantern?

297
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,360
No fire.

298
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,360
Marcel.

299
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,360
Lights, please?

300
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,360
It's hot.

301
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:54,360
Reminds me of back when I used to work in the mines.

302
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:57,360
This is...

303
00:17:58,360 --> 00:17:59,360
The stomach!

304
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:03,360
Right.

305
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,360
Here goes.

306
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:08,360
Empty.

307
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,360
But...

308
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,360
How?

309
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:11,360
Maybe it's a different dragon?

310
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:12,360
Not possible.

311
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:13,360
It has the same scar above its eye as the one we saw that day.

312
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:20,360
Male dragons are territorial, so I doubt there'd be many within the same vicinity.

313
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,360
Let's check the intestines, too.

314
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,360
No...

315
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:23,360
Not even a single bone has left it there.

316
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,360
I need to hurry and check his tongue.

317
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:28,360
Maybe it digested faster because it was moving around.

318
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,360
Hang on.

319
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:30,360
Hang on.

320
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,360
Here.

321
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:44,360
Huh?

322
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:47,580
Maybe it digested faster because it was moving around.

323
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:52,200
Hang on.

324
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,460
What is this?

325
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:16,040
A giant clump of hair and bones.

326
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:20,920
Animals that swallow their prey whole spit out the indigestible parts all at once.

327
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:25,600
However, red dragons use it as fuel for their fire breath instead.

328
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:31,460
Judging by this black fur, looks like it ate a few wargs and...

329
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:37,680
A strand of hair! Could it be?

330
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:41,240
Let's sort through it. We might find some human bones.

331
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:48,200
Hey, isn't this rod...

332
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:51,780
Laios! Look! This staff!

333
00:19:51,780 --> 00:20:00,160
Valon?

334
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:00,200
Valon?

